  "question": {
    "text": "A current-carrying wire is placed in the grooves of an insulating semicircular disc of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, as shown. The current enters at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and leaves from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>. Determine the magnetic field at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0019_eed665bb22df.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 124px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>R</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>R</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "none of these",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0019_bc7341faeeb9.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 132px;\" /></p><p>The angle formed by lines from each end of diameter to any point of the semicircle is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CB</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8869;</mo><mi>DB</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CA</mi><mo>&#8869;</mo><mi>DA</mi></math>.</p><p><br />Magnetic field due to wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AC</mi></math>,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>AC</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>sin</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mo>cos</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>cos</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><br />Magnetic field due to wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BC</mi></math>,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>BC</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mo><mo>sin</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mo>cos</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>cos</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">I</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">I</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>24</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mtext><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#8594;</mo></mover><mtext>net</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mtext><mtext>A</mtext></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mtext><mtext>B</mtext></msub></math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}